Overlay the colored contents of same-sized blank panels after removing the dominant separator color.

Input structure
- The most common color is a separator surrounding several rectangular
  panels made from a common blank color plus sparse colored marks.
- The panels are 4-connected regions of non-separator cells, and all panel
  bounding boxes have the same shape.
Rule
- Create one blank panel of that common shape.
- For each input panel, copy every non-blank mark to the same relative
  position in the output panel.
Key insight
- The large separator color is not part of the answer; the answer is the
  transparent overlay of the small drawings inside its panels.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "transform_in_place",
  "src": "same-sized rectangular panels of blank cells and colored marks separated by the dominant bg color",
  "transform": "discard the dominant separator, overlay every non-blank mark at its relative panel position on one blank panel",
  "grid_shape": "common panel height x common panel width"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 16x16 [observed]
  separator: most common color, fills everything outside panels; any non-zero color [observed]
  blank: 0 (second most common color, fills panel interiors) [observed]
  panels:
    count: 2-4
    shape: all identical, 3-5 rows x 3-5 cols
    placement: scattered freely (not grid-aligned), each fully surrounded by >=1 cell of separator, no overlap
    min_gap: >=2 separator cells between any two panels
  marks:
    per_panel: 2-5 cells of a single color, 4-connected
    colors: each panel uses a unique non-zero non-separator non-blank color
    non_overlap: mark positions (relative to panel) must not collide across panels
    coverage: union of all marks covers 45-80% of panel area [observed]

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Choose panel shape H x W (3-5 each), number of panels N (2-4), separator color (non-zero), and N distinct mark colors (all different from separator and 0).
    2. Build the output panel (H x W) by placing N connected mark blobs (one per color, 2-5 cells each) on a blank(0) background, ensuring no positional overlap. Verify marks are 4-connected per color.
    3. For each mark color, extract its cells as a separate panel patch (mark cells + blank elsewhere).
    4. Create 16x16 grid filled with separator. Place N panels (H x W) at random non-overlapping positions, each surrounded by >=1 separator border, with >=2 gap between panels. Paste each patch into its panel slot.
```
